# scoreboard: saxpy — y = 2.5 * x + y, repeated over 8M doubles.
# The chain is proven fvec (literal coefficient broadcasts), so every pass
# is ONE fused kernel: read x, read y, write y — no temporaries.
# Output contract: line 1 = checksum (sum(y)), line 2 = kernel seconds.

n = 8388608
reps = 40
x = fvec_fill(n, 1.5)
y = fvec_fill(n, 0.25)
y = 2.5 * x + y   # warm-up pass: faults the result buffer's pages
                  # outside the timed section (C variants are warmed too)
t0 = clock()
for r in range(reps):
    y = 2.5 * x + y
t1 = clock()
print(sum(y))
print(t1 - t0)
